Ze-Reviewed-Against: github.com/vishvananda/netlink v1.3.1

The state writer sends a replay window wider than 32 in
XFRMA_REPLAY_ESN_VAL, and still sets XFRM_STATE_ESN only when XfrmState.ESN
asks for it. xfrm_usersa_info.replay_window maps onto struct
xfrm_replay_state, whose bitmap is one u32, and the kernel's
copy_from_user_state (net/xfrm/xfrm_user.c) clamps the field to the 32 bits
of that bitmap without an error. Upstream sends XFRMA_REPLAY_ESN_VAL only
with ESN, so a window of 64 without ESN is installed as 32 while
XfrmStateAdd returns nil. Without XFRM_STATE_ESN, xfrm_init_replay
(net/xfrm/xfrm_replay.c) reads the attribute as a plain large bitmap
(XFRM_REPLAY_MODE_BMP). A window the kernel refuses in that attribute now
returns the kernel's error instead of being installed as 32. RFC 4303
Section 3.4.3: "A minimum window size of 32 packets MUST be supported when
32-bit sequence numbers are employed; a window size of 64 is preferred and
SHOULD be employed as the default."

No upstream pull request is opened yet for this change. Upstream issue 1213
of vishvananda/netlink ("xfrm: three bugs in state read-back, replay window
and template family", opened 2026-08-25) proposes it and has no maintainer
answer yet.

Its hunks need no earlier patch, but its upstream test reads the window
back through the reader netlink-xfrm-01-state-readback-esn-replay.patch
adds, so it is proposed after that patch.

Not yet checked against upstream main.

Delete this patch when go.mod requires an upstream release that contains the
change.

diff --git a/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_state_linux.go b/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_state_linux.go
--- a/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_state_linux.go
+++ b/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_state_linux.go
@@ -205,6 +205,10 @@
 	return mark.Serialize()
 }
 
+// xfrm_usersa_info carries a 32-bit legacy replay bitmap. Larger windows use
+// XFRMA_REPLAY_ESN_VAL; without XFRM_STATE_ESN, Linux selects bitmap mode.
+const xfrmLegacyReplayWindow = 32
+
 func writeReplayEsn(replayWindow int) []byte {
 	replayEsn := &nl.XfrmReplayStateEsn{
 		OSeq:         0,
@@ -270,11 +274,14 @@
 
 	msg := xfrmUsersaInfoFromXfrmState(state)
 
+	useReplayESN := state.ESN || state.ReplayWindow > xfrmLegacyReplayWindow
 	if state.ESN {
 		if state.ReplayWindow == 0 {
 			return fmt.Errorf("ESN flag set without ReplayWindow")
 		}
 		msg.Flags |= nl.XFRM_STATE_ESN
+	}
+	if useReplayESN {
 		msg.ReplayWindow = 0
 	}
 
@@ -307,7 +314,7 @@
 		out := nl.NewRtAttr(nl.XFRMA_MARK, writeMark(state.Mark))
 		req.AddData(out)
 	}
-	if state.ESN {
+	if useReplayESN {
 		out := nl.NewRtAttr(nl.XFRMA_REPLAY_ESN_VAL, writeReplayEsn(state.ReplayWindow))
 		req.AddData(out)
 	}
